\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.8}{\ignorespaces The successor tree for $a = 1, 2, 4, 7$; each node shows a subset and its sum. Left children add the next element, right children replace the largest element by the next one. Sums never decrease downwards, so a priority queue pops them in order: $1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 7, \ldots  $ (green: the first eight pops).}}{76}{figure.caption.104}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fracturing}{{6.8}{76}{The successor tree for $a = 1, 2, 4, 7$; each node shows a subset and its sum. Left children add the next element, right children replace the largest element by the next one. Sums never decrease downwards, so a priority queue pops them in order: $1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 7, \ldots $ (green: the first eight pops)}{figure.caption.104}{}}
